NAME
    udp - send or listen for bounded UDP datagrams

SYNOPSIS
    udp send [--source-port PORT] ADDRESS PORT [TEXT...]
    udp listen PORT

DESCRIPTION
    Sends one checksummed datagram from a persistent ephemeral or selected
    source port, using standard input when TEXT is omitted. listen persistently
    binds PORT and waits cooperatively for its oldest queued datagram. Each of
    at most eight ports retains four datagrams and 4 KiB; newest input is
    dropped at capacity. Ctrl-C cancels the wait. DNS and general sockets are
    not part of this command.
